<title>UK: Sun Life and Prov Irish unit sales rise.</title>
<headline>Sun Life and Prov Irish unit sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sun Life and Provincial Holdings said on Tuesday that its Irish subsidiary New Ireland Assurance had recorded an 18 percent increase in its insurance premium to 21.8 million Irish pounds in 1996.</p>
<p>Sun Life said New Ireland's pensions business was worth 11.1 million punts which rose 26 percent. Life annual premiums rose 11 percent to 10.7 million punts.</p>
<p>Single premium income rose 31 percent to 120.4 million punts.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
